      "writtenOn": "2022-06-21T20:00:18Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hi Tim,\nPractically, adapter rating cannot go beyond of maximum of 100 -200 Watts , which means 200,000 mW, which is within 32 bits. So, overflow of 32 bits is not practically possible is my guess! Now, reasoning behind rating in  50mW units: suppose 200,000mW , it crosses [0:15] bits to 17th bit. so to limit the value within [0:15] bits, division by 50.  I agree that adapter rating in Watts would have saved some 8 bits of memory on EC side, but looks like Power Boss Action Table probably has a dependency on the accurate value adapter rating in MW itself. To quote an example, suppose, if we use a low power charging cable like suzyQ, then adapter rating would be 7500mW (1500mA /5000mV). If we prefer to save it in terms of watts only , then EC would report it as 7Watts instead of 7.5 Watts.",
